## 3. Security‑hardening middleware

| Concern | Middleware | What it does |
|---------|------------|--------------|
| HTTP security headers | `helmet` | Sets `Content‑Security‑Policy`, `X‑Frame‑Options`, `X‑XSS‑Protection`, etc. |
| Rate limiting | `express-rate-limit` | Throttles abusive IPs (e.g., 100 req/min). |
| CORS restriction | `cors` | Whitelists origins you actually serve. |
| Body size limits | `express.json({ limit: '10kb' })` | Prevents huge payload attacks. |
| Prevent parameter pollution | `hpp` | Removes duplicate query parameters. |

```js
const helmet = require('helmet');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const cors = require('cors');
const hpp = require('hpp');

app.use(helmet());

app.use(
  rateLimit({
    windowMs: 60 * 1000, // 1 minute
    max: 100, // limit each IP to 100 requests per window
    standardHeaders: true,
    legacyHeaders: false,
  })
);

app.use(cors({
  origin: ['https://mytrusteddomain.com'], // adjust to your front‑ends
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'OPTIONS'],
}));

app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' })); // parses JSON bodies
app.use(hpp()); // protects against HTTP Parameter Pollution
```

