## 5. Graceful shutdown & unhandled‑rejection handling

Unexpected rejections can leave the process in an inconsistent state. Capture them and exit cleanly (or restart via a process manager like PM2).

```js
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
  // decide whether to exit or keep running
  // process.exit(1);
});

process.on('uncaughtException', err => {
  console.error('Uncaught Exception:', err);
  // perform any cleanup then exit
  // process.exit(1);
});
```

