## 1. General Structure & Configuration

| Issue | Why it matters | Fix / Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|-----------------------|
| **Hard‑coded port** (`3000`) | Makes it difficult to run the same code in different environments (dev, prod, CI) and may expose the app on an unintended interface. | Use an environment variable (`process.env.PORT`) with a sane default. |
| **No CORS configuration** | By default Express will allow any origin when you later add `res.json`. If you ever expose the API to browsers, an open‑origin policy is a risk. | Add the **cors** middleware and whitelist only the origins you need. |
| **No security‑related HTTP headers** | Missing protections against click‑jacking, XSS, MIME‑sniffing, etc. | Install and use **helmet** (`app.use(helmet())`). |
| **No request‑size limits** | An attacker could send extremely large payloads (if you later add POST bodies) and exhaust memory. | Use `express.json({ limit: '10kb' })` (or appropriate limit). |
| **No rate limiting** | Brute‑force or denial‑of‑service attacks can hammer the health endpoint or any future POST routes. | Add **express‑rate‑limit**. |
| **No centralized error handling** | Uncaught errors will cause the server to crash or leak stack traces to the client. | Add an error‑handling middleware that logs the error and returns a generic message. |
| **No logging** | Without request/error logs you’ll have a hard time troubleshooting or detecting abuse. | Use **morgan** (or a more powerful logger like **winston/pino**). |

### Example – Core Middleware Stack

```js
// config.js (optional)
module.exports = {
  port: process.env.PORT || 3000,
  corsOrigins: process.env.CORS_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['https://myapp.com'],
};

// app.js (excerpt)
const express = require('express');
const helmet = require('helmet');
const cors = require('cors');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const morgan = require('morgan');

const { port, corsOrigins } = require('./config');
const app = express();

// 1️⃣ Security headers
app.use(helmet());

// 2️⃣ CORS (whitelist)
app.use(cors({
  origin: function (origin, callback) {
    // allow requests with no origin (like mobile apps, curl)  
    if (!origin) return callback(null, true);
    if (corsOrigins.includes(origin)) return callback(null, true);
    callback(new Error('Not allowed by CORS'));
  }
}));

// 3️⃣ Body parsing (JSON) – size limit
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' })); // adjust as needed

// 4️⃣ Rate limiting – per IP, per minute
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 60 * 1000, // 1 minute
  max: 100, // limit each IP to 100 requests per windowMs
  standardHeaders: true,
  legacyHeaders: false,
});
app.use(limiter);

// 5️⃣ HTTP request logging
app.use(morgan('combined'));
```

