## 10. Checklist for the Future  

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| **Helmet** enabled |
| **Rate limiting** configured |
| **Trust proxy** set in production (if behind a reverse proxy) |
| **Input validation** (Joi/Zod) for every new route |
| **Async error wrapper** (`asyncHandler`) used everywhere |
| **Centralized error middleware** – no stack traces in prod |
| **404 handler** added |
| **Environment‑based config** (`dotenv`, `PORT`, `LOG_LEVEL`) |
| **Structured logging** (pino/winston) |
| **Dependency audit** integrated in CI |
| **Response size limits** (`express.json({ limit })`) |
| **No sensitive data in logs** |
| **Pagination / filtering** on collection endpoints |
| **HTTPS enforcement** (redirect or HSTS) if you terminate TLS |

By implementing the above changes you’ll significantly improve the security posture of the application, make debugging easier, and lay a solid foundation for any future features you add. Feel free to ask if you’d like help wiring a specific validator, integrating a database, or setting up CI‑based security scans!
